cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WRRA-M 0.2, please cite this research note."
title: "WRRA-M 0.2: Cross-Dimensional Filter Correspondence"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Choi
    given-names: Wonsik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4263-9772"
    email: "janefather@gmail.com"
version: "0.2"
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
url: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
abstract: >-
  WRRA-M 0.2 defines a sixteen-channel space consisting of one invariant
  channel, two seven-dimensional sectors, and one null channel. A conditional
  cross-dimensional filter reorganizes the space into the Pati-Salam
  representation (4,2,1) plus (anti-4,1,2). Neutrality of the null channel and
  unit normalization of the invariant channel fix the hypercharge operator
  Y = T3R + (B-L)/2. The one-generation hypercharges, electric charges, local
  anomalies, mixed gravitational anomaly, and global SU(2) parity conditions
  then close. The existence and dynamics of the filter are not derived.
keywords:
  - WRRA
  - Wonsik Reality Renderer Architecture
  - meta-dimensional
  - predimensional degrees
  - cross-dimensional filter
  - Pati-Salam
  - SO(10)
  - G2
  - Standard Model
  - hypercharge
  - anomaly cancellation
